ollection Framework is a set of classes and interfaces
 in Java that is used to store,
 manage, and manipulate a group of objects efficiently.

Why do we need Collection Framework?

Arrays have fixed size

No ready-made methods like add, delete, search

Collections solve these problems



Main parts of Collection Framework
1️⃣ Interfaces

They define rules / structure
List – allows duplicates (ArrayList, LinkedList)
Set – no duplicates (HashSet, TreeSet)
Queue – follows order (PriorityQueue)
Map – key-value pairs (HashMap, TreeMap)

2️⃣ Classes

They provide implementation

ArrayList
LinkedList
HashSet
HashMap
TreeSet

3️⃣ Algorithms

Utility methods from Collections class
sort()
reverse()
shuffle()
max() / min()
